# Tests, fixtures, seeds, coverage

Noche Live is a new Rails app. Untested code is unfinished.

```text
test/                 Minitest for every class, service, and controller action
test/fixtures/*.yml   YAML fixtures for every ActiveRecord model
db/seeds.rb           Idempotent playable DEMO night
SimpleCov             full `bin/rails test` and CI must stay ≥ 90% of app/
```

## Do

- Ship tests in the same change as the behavior.
- Add a fixture file when adding a model. Use labels (`game_sessions(:david)`).
- Keep `db/seeds.rb` able to demo the night after `bin/rails db:seed`.
- Run the full suite before finishing a slice. If coverage drops below 90%, write tests first.
- Put use-case tests in `test/services/` once services exist.

## Do not

- Add RSpec or FactoryBot as a substitute for `test/` + YAML fixtures.
- Skip tests because the slice is small.
- Lower the SimpleCov threshold or filter production code to game coverage.
- Leave `db/seeds.rb` as the Rails comment stub.
